  "summary": "HMS Dolphin sailed to find the southern continent, went through the Strait of Magellan and across the Tuamotus, and on 18 June 1767 sighted Tahiti. Wallis anchored in Matavai Bay, where canoes attacked the ship, which fired its guns, and then stayed five weeks, trading iron for food and meeting the chiefess Purea. He claimed Tahiti for Britain and sailed on to Tinian; the way home by Batavia and the Cape, to the Downs on 20 May 1768, is not drawn.",
